// Your greeting's settings: ~/.config/kubaos/terminal/fastfetch/greeting.jsonc, merged over
// KubaOS's greeting (the short list a new Ghostty window shows; objects key by key, anything
// else replaces ours). dot-config apply, which every update runs, writes
// ~/.config/fastfetch/greeting.jsonc from both: run it after editing. `fastfetch` on its own
// reads config.jsonc beside this file.
{
  // The lines shown, in order. Each module you add costs time before the prompt shows: the
  // GPU's alone takes about 150 ms.
  // "modules": ["title", "separator", "os", "kernel", "uptime", "memory"]

  // Full docs: https://github.com/fastfetch-cli/fastfetch/wiki/Configuration
}
